e1e5cce1d932f298.abstract:
Joint with Masato Tsujii, we show that any C^r diffeomorphism that is sufficiently close to the time-1 map of a C^r generic volume-preserving 3D Anosov flow (for some absolute constant r) is topologically mixing and has a unique Gibbs state. This gives:
the first answer to a question of Palis-Pugh in 1974 on the approximability of time-1 maps of transitive Anosov flow by Axiom A diffeomorphisms;
the first robustly transitive diffeomorphism (in C^r topology for some r) without periodic points.

